    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0107" n="941" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg941"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/484</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-15T21:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1918, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6261. Following for Sheldon from War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>Our No. 10. In connection with the doing away of letters of assurance, please
                    report to us your recommendations as to the plan for division of rations, as
                    between Great Britain, United States, and other countries.</p>
                <p> McCormick discussed this matter with you when in London, but desires you to
                    submit your complete and detailed recommendations upon this subject, in order
                    that we can all agree upon a policy and thereby avoid friction in the
                    future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
